omap_spi: receive-only words start on the TX write, not on channel enable

In receive-only mode (TRM = 1) the model clocked a word whenever the
channel was enabled. McSPI starts the first receive-only word with a
(dummy) write to MCSPI_TX, which Linux's omap2-mcspi does after enabling
the channel; later words start when MCSPI_RX is read with the channel
enabled. Linux also re-enables the channel after the last read, so the
model clocked an extra word there, dropping a response byte. With the
N810 panel (MIPID on McSPI1) the display ID read back as 00 83 8f
instead of 83 8f 03.

diff --git a/hw/ssi/omap_spi.c b/hw/ssi/omap_spi.c
index 8f85c3e39..dd2f25dce 100644
--- a/hw/ssi/omap_spi.c
+++ b/hw/ssi/omap_spi.c
@@ -315,7 +315,10 @@ static void omap_mcspi_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr,
     case 0x48: ch ++;
         /* fall through */
     case 0x34:	/* MCSPI_CHCTRL */
-        if (value & ~s->ch[ch].control & 1) {		/* EN */
+        /* In receive-only mode the first word starts with a (dummy)
+         * write to MCSPI_TX, not with the channel enable.  */
+        if ((value & ~s->ch[ch].control & 1) &&		/* EN */
+                        ((s->ch[ch].config >> 12) & 3) != 1) {	/* TRM */
             s->ch[ch].control |= 1;
             omap_mcspi_transfer_run(s, ch);
         } else
